            <ArticleTitle>Verapamil therapy for persistent antral spasms in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>529-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Little is known about the use of calcium channel blockers in children with gastric motility disorders. We report the case of an 11-year-old child who was hospitalized after 3 weeks of persistent vomiting, abdominal pain, and a 12-lb weight loss. When his symptoms failed to improve with traditional treatment, verapamil therapy was begun. Within 24 hours, his symptoms totally resolved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
